<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore March M1 rises 9.8 pct on year - MAS.</title>
<headline>Singapore March M1 rises 9.8 pct on year - MAS.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Money supply figures.</p>
<p>	   (in billions of Singapore dollars)</p>
<p>			    Mar     Feb	Mar '96</p>
<p>M-1 (narrow money)   28.47    27.92    25.93</p>
<p>M-2		     117.03   113.66   104.72</p>
<p>M-3 (broad money)   145.10   141.87   131.18</p>
<p>Demand deposits	17.74    17.06    15.91</p>
<p>Currency in active   10.73    10.86    10.01</p>
<p>circulation  </p>
<p>Note - The Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) said narrow money supply (M1) grew by 9.8 percent year-on-year in March compared with 6.9 percent in February.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
